WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.600
Symphony helps you connect what matters in your

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.580
life with what you need to do today.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.270
In Symphony, you can break a big goal

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.190
into smaller goals, then choose tasks that help

5
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:10.870
you achieve them.

6
00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:13.475
Start with whatever’s on your mind.

7
00:00:14.295 --> 00:00:18.055
Press Command-K or Control-K, or tap the circle-plus

8
00:00:18.055 --> 00:00:20.895
button, to capture a thought, task, or idea

9
00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:21.595
in your Inbox.

10
00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:24.455
You don’t need to organize it right away.

11
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.855
Later, decide whether it’s something to do, a

12
00:00:27.855 --> 00:00:30.355
goal to work toward, or information to keep

13
00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:32.575
— and add any details you’ll need.

14
00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.150
Symphony gives you five places to plan.

15
00:00:36.922 --> 00:00:38.322
The year is for your bigger goals.

16
00:00:39.222 --> 00:00:41.062
The season and month help you decide what

17
00:00:41.062 --> 00:00:41.942
to focus on next.

18
00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:44.762
The week is where you choose your commitments,

19
00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:46.922
and today is where you get to work.

20
00:00:47.722 --> 00:00:49.202
You can start wherever you need to.

21
00:00:49.842 --> 00:00:52.282
Let’s follow one family goal through all five.

22
00:00:53.222 --> 00:00:54.802
Suppose your goal for the year is to

23
00:00:54.802 --> 00:00:56.822
spend more quality time as a family.

24
00:00:57.762 --> 00:00:59.902
For the season, you make that more specific:

25
00:01:00.762 --> 00:01:03.142
build a habit of spending time outdoors together.

26
00:01:04.102 --> 00:01:06.962
This month, you set a smaller goal: go

27
00:01:06.962 --> 00:01:09.382
on two family walks, and pick the two

28
00:01:09.382 --> 00:01:10.402
days you’d like to go.

29
00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:13.692
To make the first walk happen, you add

30
00:01:13.692 --> 00:01:16.672
a task to this week’s plan: choose a

31
00:01:16.672 --> 00:01:17.932
trail for Saturday’s walk.

32
00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:21.352
When you’re ready to choose the trail, add

33
00:01:21.352 --> 00:01:22.492
that task to Today.

34
00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:25.632
Open it, compare the trail links you’ve saved

35
00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:27.452
alongside it, and choose one.

36
00:01:29.309 --> 00:01:31.449
Of course, not everything starts with a bigger

37
00:01:31.449 --> 00:01:31.709
goal.

38
00:01:32.989 --> 00:01:35.149
Sometimes, something just needs your attention today.

39
00:01:36.349 --> 00:01:38.649
Suppose the pharmacy hasn't filled a medication you

40
00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:38.789
need.

41
00:01:39.529 --> 00:01:41.009
You can add a task to today.

42
00:01:41.669 --> 00:01:43.469
Call the pharmacy about my missing medication.

43
00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:47.749
You or Symphony’s AI can prepare the details

44
00:01:47.749 --> 00:01:51.669
beforehand: the correct store’s verified phone number, which

45
00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:54.429
medication is missing, and any notes from your

46
00:01:54.429 --> 00:01:55.269
last conversation.

47
00:01:56.109 --> 00:01:58.789
When you’re ready, open the task and tap

48
00:01:58.789 --> 00:01:59.589
the number to call.

49
00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:01.569
The details are right there.

50
00:02:02.449 --> 00:02:06.369
Afterward, record the answer and add any follow-up.

51
00:02:06.775 --> 00:02:08.275
That takes care of the unexpected.

52
00:02:09.615 --> 00:02:11.995
For the jobs that come around regularly, routines

53
00:02:11.995 --> 00:02:14.195
help your family keep track of who’s responsible.

54
00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:17.135
Add taking out the trash as a Tuesday

55
00:02:17.135 --> 00:02:19.615
routine, then choose who will handle it.

56
00:02:20.815 --> 00:02:23.435
Assign it to a particular family member, or

57
00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:25.135
leave it open for anyone to take care

58
00:02:25.135 --> 00:02:25.435
of.

59
00:02:25.435 --> 00:02:28.715
The assignment appears with the task, and when

60
00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:31.475
it’s marked done, everyone sees that it’s finished.

61
00:02:32.475 --> 00:02:34.135
At the end of the week, take a

62
00:02:34.135 --> 00:02:35.695
few minutes to look back at what you

63
00:02:35.695 --> 00:02:38.035
finished and decide what to do with anything

64
00:02:38.035 --> 00:02:38.595
unfinished.

65
00:02:39.835 --> 00:02:41.255
If you still need to choose a trail

66
00:02:41.255 --> 00:02:43.575
for the family walk, you can carry that

67
00:02:43.575 --> 00:02:44.755
task into next week.

68
00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.707
If researching a new tent can wait, save

69
00:02:47.707 --> 00:02:48.187
it in Someday.

70
00:02:49.347 --> 00:02:50.827
And if you’ve decided to keep an item

71
00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:52.607
you purchased, you can let go of the

72
00:02:52.607 --> 00:02:53.667
task to return it.

73
00:02:54.847 --> 00:02:57.967
Unfinished tasks don’t automatically become next week’s commitments.

74
00:02:59.027 --> 00:03:00.847
You choose what still deserves your time.
